//
// offload-mode gate: the D2 layer partitioned by LINEARITY.
//
// `[2026-08-08]` Rewritten for the corrected taxonomy. The four modes span
// reconfiguration cost against DRAM traffic, not "who sequences the work", and
// offload is the mode that MINIMIZES reconfiguration -- with every LINEAR
// operator on the NPU and every NON-LINEAR one on the host. See 03 The taxonomy.
// The version of this file before that correction required
// "attention host torch fp32" and pinned six dispatches: it certified the
// obsolete implementation and would have passed the wrong build.
//
// So: eight linear operators over five compiled shapes. The six projections
// resolve in the registry; the two attention matmuls resolve in NO registry and
// cannot be swept into one (sweep_families.py derives K and N from
// FAMILY_HIDDEN x ROLE_KN_MULTIPLES with a minimum hidden of 512, so no family
// puts a 64 in the K or N slot). That is a CATALOGUE constraint, not a hardware
// one -- both shapes are measured passing on real NPU2 -- and their tiles are
// injected through the gemm_spec_fn escape hatch every builder ships. Only the
// softmax between the two attention matmuls, both norms and the GeLU stay on
// the host, written independently of the numpy oracle.
//
// Two recipes in one file, deliberately: they share a working directory and
// therefore the ELF cache, so the injected run reuses the five ELFs the clean
// run compiled -- compilation depends on the shape, not the data.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipes below: device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock inside KernelCache, the same inode
// lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution takes. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock
// here would DEADLOCK against the gate command that already holds it -- BSD
// flock(2) treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_offload_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_offload_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-offload PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// The configuration first -- the forced gate configuration, each projection
// resolved through the registry, and the mode's own statement that attention is
// now on the device. A registry change that moved a method fails here with its
// cause on screen.
// CHECK: offload 4096x768 ffn 3072 12h x 64 (encoder_bert, non-causal, linear boundary: 8 linear operators over 5 shapes, 30 dispatches, attention on device)
// CHECK: proj 4096x768x768 drain (registry), up 4096x768x3072 drain (registry), down 4096x3072x768 fused-cast (registry)
//
// The INJECTED tiles in full. These two lines are the whole reason the mode can
// put attention on the device, and they are the one place a reader sees that
// these tiles came from a measurement rather than from a lookup. Each is the
// configuration that passed on hardware at 0% allowed mismatch over the full
// output: attn_scores at mean_rel_L1 9.386e-3 (tk2=64 is forced -- K=64 admits
// no other L2 tile), attn_output at 9.417e-3 with a 3.46x margin. A silent
// retune to a faster or narrower configuration fails right here.
// CHECK: attn_scores 4096x64x4096 drain tk2=64 tk1=32 tn=128 herd 8x4 (injected), attn_output 4096x4096x64 drain tk2=256 tk1=32 tn=16 herd 8x4 (injected)
// CHECK: attention on device: 2 GEMMs x 12 heads = 24 dispatches, host keeps scale + softmax
//
// Every boundary, in execution order, each with zero mismatching elements.
// Named individually rather than counted, so a stage list that dropped or
// repeated an entry fails here -- the driver requires at least eight DISTINCT
// names, and this is where the suite enforces the same thing.
// CHECK: [stage] q {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] k {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] v {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] attn_context {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] attn_out {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] hidden {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] ffn_up {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] ffn_gelu {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] ffn_out {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [stage] output {{.*}} mismatch       0
// CHECK: [offload] stages: 10/10 clean
//
// The mode's own instrumentation: one DispatchVector row per dispatch. Thirty
// -- six projections plus two attention matmuls on each of twelve heads. A
// wrapper that batched the per-head pairs into one runlist, or stopped
// recording per-dispatch rows, fails here before the driver's totals
// comparison sees it.
// CHECK: [offload] recorded 30 dispatch vectors
//
// The vectors' CONTENTS, not only their count.
//
// WHERE THESE NUMBERS COME FROM, because it decides what a failure means.
// submissions / entries / air / sync / bytes are DERIVED, from a per-dispatch
// model: bytes = A + B + C plus a f32 C scratch for fused-cast, one air launch
// per drain dispatch and two for fused-cast, three sync boundaries per drain
// dispatch (A and B up, C back) and four for fused-cast. That model reproduces
// the SIX-dispatch line this gate pinned before the rewrite exactly -- air 7,
// sync 19, bytes 139984896 -- which is what made it safe to extend to thirty
// rather than a guess dressed as a literal. herd is the one field the model
// could NOT derive; it was left as a regex until the first clean run, which
// returned 91, and every derived field came back exactly as predicted.
//
// bytes is 970457088: 926 MiB against the 134 MiB the six-dispatch form moved,
// a 6.9x increase. That is NOT a regression to fix. A host softmax between two
// device matmuls means the full 4096x4096 score matrix crosses DRAM twice per
// head, and pricing exactly that is what the mode is for.
// CHECK: [offload] dispatch totals: submissions 30 entries 30 air 31 herd 91 sync 91 bytes 970457088
//
// THE MODE'S OWN AXIS ON THIS PATH, and it was unpinned until `[2026-08-09]`.
// The six fields above cannot carry it: they are identical whether the array is
// configured once or thirty times, because the mode makes one run_sequence call
// per GEMM either way. This is the ELF path, so thirty is CORRECT here -- each
// dispatch evicts and reloads its hw_context (see _evict_context). Pinning it
// is what makes the two paths distinguishable in the suite rather than only in
// prose: without this line a build that silently switched packaging would pass
// green on both recipes.
// CHECK: [offload] reconfiguration: context_loads 30 kernel_attaches 0 over 30 dispatches
//
// Then the layer output itself over all 4096 x 768 elements, and the label
// naming the MODE's operator.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] offload [4096x768_encoder_bert]: PASS
//
// THE NEGATIVE CONTROL. Identical reasoning to the block gate's -- ln1_weight,
// chosen by measurement, perturbed AFTER the golden model was computed -- plus
// the one stake that is this mode's own: the dispatch vectors must be recorded
// on the injected path too, because the driver requires the fault artifact's
// summed totals to EQUAL the clean run's.
//
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-offload-fault PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAULT
//
// The injected element first, so an injection that silently perturbed nothing
// is visible here rather than read backwards from the verdict. Index 5 is
// ln1_weight in OFFLOAD_INPUT_NAMES -- the q/k/v weights are separate in this
// mode, so the index differs from the block's.
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 5 at (0,)
//
// Nothing upstream of the first norm reads ln1_weight, so the attention half
// must still be exact while `hidden` and everything after it moves -- which is
// what says the stage comparisons are reading THIS run's buffers rather than
// replaying the clean run's. attn_context is now produced by two DEVICE GEMMs
// rather than by host torch, so this clause also says the device attention path
// is exact on the run where the layer's verdict is FAIL.
// FAULT: [stage] q {{.*}} mismatch       0
// FAULT: [stage] attn_context {{.*}} mismatch       0
// FAULT: [stage] attn_out {{.*}} mismatch       0
// FAULT: [stage] hidden {{.*}} mismatch {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
// FAULT: [offload] stages: 5/10 clean
//
// The vectors, still recorded under injection -- and totaling EXACTLY what
// the clean run totals: the literals below are the same ones the clean half
// pins above, which is the suite's own statement of the equality the driver
// re-derives from the two artifacts.
// FAULT: [offload] recorded 30 dispatch vectors
// FAULT: [offload] dispatch totals: submissions 30 entries 30 air 31 herd 91 sync 91 bytes 970457088
//
// And the verdict in the three forms opcheck.py reports it: the comparison's
// own, the control's reading of it, and the exit-status summary.
// FAULT: [opcheck] offload [4096x768_encoder_bert]: FAIL
// FAULT: [opcheck] offload [4096x768_encoder_bert]: fault-inject input -> FAIL (as required)
// FAULT: NEGATIVE CONTROL: PASS
//
// ===========================================================================
// THE SHARED-XCLBIN PATH -- the half of this mode's definition that was
// PRINTED AND NOT ENFORCED until `[2026-08-09]`.
//
// doc 03 defines offload as "reconfiguration MINIMIZED by dynamic
// partitioning", and doc 29 landed the mechanism: five GEMM shapes chained into
// ONE xclbin, loaded once, each binding its own kernel and instruction stream
// onto the standing context. Nothing in this suite ran that path. Its central
// claim -- context_loads 1 against the ELF path's 30 -- was reported by a print
// statement, so a regression to thirty loads would have passed every gate here
// green while the mode quietly stopped being the mode.
//
// WHY THIS RECIPE IS AT 1024 WHEN THE TWO ABOVE ARE AT 4096, measured rather
// than chosen. The chain does not build at 4096. At 4096 the down-projection
// resolves to `fused-cast`, which is TWO air.launch ops; every other shape at
// either length is single-launch `drain`. XRTBackend.compile defaults its
// instruction file to the fixed name air.insts.bin and the xclbin branch passes
// it straight through, while the ELF branch passes an elf name and no
// instruction flag at all -- so only the ELF path lets aircc derive a name per
// launch. A two-launch module under the xclbin ABI therefore asks aiecc to
// write every instruction stream to one path, and aiecc refuses:
// "edge 'air.insts.bin' produced duplicate output path". The shared path is
// bounded to SINGLE-LAUNCH modules today. 1024 is where all five shapes are
// single-launch, and it is the shape doc 29 demonstrated -- which nothing in
// that document said, because it never ran the other one.
//
// So this recipe enforces the claim WHERE THE CLAIM HOLDS, and the 4096 wall is
// recorded in doc 29 as its own item rather than left as an unexplained gap.
//
// It runs through study/run_mode.py rather than opcheck.py because the sequence
// length is the whole point here and only run_mode takes one; opcheck reads its
// shape from the SPECS row, and adding a second offload row to move it would
// churn the 4096 row that is gated, provenanced and cited across three
// documents. run_mode still compares every boundary against the same golden
// reference at the same row's atol and still reports a status, so this is a
// correctness check and not only a counter check. No fault recipe accompanies
// it: the shared path changes PACKAGING, not arithmetic, and the negative
// control above already covers the arithmetic.
//
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-offload-shared PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SHARED
//
// The mode's own statement of what it built, first -- so a run that fell back
// to per-artifact xclbins fails here, before any counter is read.
// SHARED: reconfiguration: ONE xclbin over 5 shapes, 30 dispatches share 1 hw_context
//
// Every boundary clean at this length too. The shared path must be numerically
// indistinguishable from the ELF one: it changes how the array is configured,
// not what it computes, so any drift here means the chain bound a kernel to the
// wrong instruction stream -- the failure mode doc 29 records as silent, where
// a colliding kernel id returned garbage at mean_rel_L1 1.41 with no error.
// SHARED: [stage] q {{.*}} mismatch       0
// SHARED: [stage] attn_context {{.*}} mismatch       0
// SHARED: [stage] output {{.*}} mismatch       0
// SHARED: [offload] stages: 10/10 clean
//
// The dispatch vector at this length, pinned to literals. The mode makes one
// run_sequence call per GEMM whichever way it is packaged, and that equality is
// MEASURED rather than assumed: the ELF path run at this same length reports
// submissions 30 entries 30 air 30 herd 90 sync 90 bytes 99090432, field for
// field the line below, and doc 27's ladder records the same 99090432. What
// this line ENFORCES is that the shared path's own structure does not drift,
// which is the regression that would otherwise be invisible.
//
// A COLD DISPATCH DOES NOT PRODUCE THESE NUMBERS, and the target dispatches
// twice for that reason. Under the xclbin ABI the first call uploads each
// artifact's INSTRUCTION stream once -- five artifacts, five extra sync
// boundaries, exactly 51,088 bytes, which is the total size of the five cached
// insts files. The ELF ABI skips that entirely, because an ELF embeds its
// instructions, and its first dispatch already reads the steady state.
//
// BOTH lines are pinned, cold first and steady second, so each check is
// anchored to a known invocation. Pinning only the steady one would leave the
// checks free to match whichever dispatch happened to agree, and a second
// dispatch that regressed could be skipped over.
// SHARED: [offload] dispatch totals: submissions 30 entries 30 air 30 herd 90 sync 95 bytes 99141520
// SHARED: [offload] dispatch totals: submissions 30 entries 30 air 30 herd 90 sync 90 bytes 99090432
//
// AND THE CLAIM ITSELF. One context load for thirty dispatches, with four
// kernels attached onto the standing configuration -- against thirty loads and
// zero attaches on the ELF path pinned in the clean half above. This single
// line is what this recipe exists for.
//
// The counter is CUMULATIVE over the cache's life, and the two paths therefore
// diverge with every layer rather than by a constant. Measured over this
// target's two dispatches of the layer: the ELF path reads context_loads 30
// after the first and 60 after the second, while the shared path reads 1 after
// both. So the check below is also insensitive to how many times the target
// dispatches, where the clean half's `context_loads 30` is a single-dispatch
// figure and would read 60 if opcheck ever dispatched twice.
// SHARED: [offload] reconfiguration: context_loads 1 kernel_attaches 4 over 30 dispatches
//
// The run's own verdict last, so none of the above can pass on a run that
// failed its comparison.
// SHARED: [run-mode] offload @ 1024x768_encoder_bert: passed
